==Battleground==
*4 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ragin' Gory|Ragin' Gories]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
*1 [[Suidae Piggicus]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Casaurian Ahirujo]]s spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is surprisingly easy. A constant spawn of [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] along with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] can handle all Behemoth enemies here quite well. There is a very long gap between 2 Metal Doge spawns so you can use any disposable unit with Critical ability to take care of it, such as [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]].

